-- title:
--   Hasse root as exponent-two Kummer generator in characteristic 3
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic $3$ and let $M$ be a nonzero natural number. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\kappa$, that is, a package consisting of a modular form $w.\mathrm{form}$ of weight $1$ for the image of $\Gamma_1(M)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, a power series $w.\mathrm{series} \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ whose image under $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}$ is the width-one $q$-expansion of $w.\mathrm{form}$, and the requirement that $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\ \kappa\ w.\mathrm{series}$ — the Laurent series over $\kappa$ obtained by reducing the coefficients of $w.\mathrm{series}$ into $\kappa$ and regarding the result as an element of $\kappa((q))$ — is nonzero. Set $a := (\mathrm{intSeriesC}\ \kappa\ w.\mathrm{series})^{-1} \in \kappa((q))$, the Hasse root function of $w$, and let $K_0 := \mathrm{x1FunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M$ be the intermediate field of $\kappa((q))/\kappa$ generated by the set $\mathrm{intFormRatiosC}\ \kappa\ (\Gamma_1(M))$ of reduced ratios of integral $q$-expansions for $\Gamma_1(M)$. The conclusion is that $a$ is a Kummer generator of exponent $2$ over $K_0$ in the sense of the project's predicate: $0 < 2$, $a \neq 0$, and $a^{2} \in K_0$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$3$ instance of the statement that the reciprocal of the reduced $q$-expansion of an integral weight-one form generates a Kummer extension of exponent $p-1$ of the function field of $X_1(M)$; at $p=3$ the exponent is $2$, and the relation $a^2 = \bar E_6/(\bar p_1^{\,2}\bar E_4)$ replaces the nonexistent level-one form of weight $p-1=2$. It feeds the results on powers of the Hasse root lying in the Igusa function field, on separability and finiteness of that extension, and on Gauss reduction for small primes.
